    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate with **Corbin Carroll** standing as the clear anchor of our offense. With an elite efficiency score of 73.877, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a favorable matchup against Junis, bolstered by an 8% boost for holding down the #2 spot in the order. Despite a minor penalty for the scarcity risk associated with his aggressive base-stealing profile, his ability to manipulate the game in all five categories makes him our highest-floor play. **Josh Naylor** also projects as a strong start at 65.49, capitalizing on the platoon advantage against Lambert to secure a top-tier score. While **Gabriel Moreno** and **Cole Young** are in the lineup, they hover closer to the marginal range; **Gabriel Moreno**\u2019s score is suppressed by his spot in the 8-hole, though he maintains enough upside to avoid the bench.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was benching **Travis Bazzana**. With a score of 38.05, **Travis Bazzana** fell just short of our 40.0 \"Zebras\" floor. While his underlying xwOBA of .394 suggests he is hitting the ball well, the severe platoon disadvantage against Suter combined with a bottom-third order placement makes him too risky to start given our current game-cap management strategy. We are also monitoring the availability of **Jose Caballero**, **James Wood**, and **Mickey Moniak**, all of whom are sidelined by team off-days or rest today. As we look ahead, we remain cautious about the weather and potential late-inning shifts for **Trevor Story**, **Brice Turang**, and **Seiya Suzuki**, but for today, the focus remains on extracting maximum value from **Austin Riley**, **Giancarlo Stanton**, **Vinnie Pasquantino**, **Tyler Soderstrom**, **Max Muncy**, **Carson Williams**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Kyle Karros**, **Luis Campusano**, and **Alex Freeland** as they navigate their respective matchups.",
